; tls, assembled: each part a (module 'tls form, so the parts register the one
; module and the loader keeps the file-made registration -- sb's and lush's shape.
; bytes is first because it is the floor the rest index with; verify reads the server's key
; and its signature, and the client stands on all of them. p256 signs and cert writes
; certificates. the aead's ciphers are src/love/crypto/tls.c's nifs, and their love oracles
; are the laws' (test/host/chacha.l, test/host/poly1305.l).
(borrow "src/apps/tls/bytes.l")
(borrow "src/apps/tls/verify.l")
(borrow "src/apps/tls/client.l")
(borrow "src/apps/tls/p256.l")
(borrow "src/apps/tls/cert.l")
